    {
      "id": "camera_housing",
      "title": "Rear camera housing",
      "type": "list",
      "intro": "Separate from the box and the tray. Source: `hardware/cad/camera_housing.py` (parts: housing, lid and rack clamp cap; plate `camera_plate.3mf`; native FreeCAD versions in `hardware/freecad/models/`). Raspberry Pi Camera Module 3 Wide, sized from the official Raspberry Pi mechanical drawing, films backwards from under the back end of the rear rack.",
      "items": [
        "Camera Module 3 Wide (official drawing): board 25 x 23.862 mm, PCB 1.12 mm; holes 2.2 mm (4.75 mm pads), 21 mm apart across and 12.5 mm apart up, the lower pair 2.0 mm above the bottom edge and 2.0 mm in from the sides; lens centred across, 14.4 mm above the bottom edge; square lens block 10.8 x 10.8 x 4.07 mm, round barrel 6.95 mm, lens tip 8.3 mm in front of the PCB; whole module 12 mm deep (2.58 mm behind the PCB); ribbon connector 19.61 x 5.71 mm on the back at the top edge. Field of view 102 deg across, 67 deg up, 120 deg diagonal.",
        "Housing 44.8 x 26.1 x 41.8 mm with its side rails (50.2 mm wide with the lock bars on), lid 3.5 mm plus four pegs, a locating lip and two side flanges, two lock bars 4.9 x 12 x 38.7 mm, cap 20 x 26.7 x 10.5 mm; about 54 mm tall with the cap. These follow from the parameters: the depth is set by the clamp (rack tube 10 mm guessed), not the camera.",
        "Camera sits ribbon-down (connector at the bottom edge) on four 4.4 mm diameter posts with 1.8 mm pins through its holes; the four lid pegs press it on. The lens barrel reaches into a 7.75 mm bore in the 6.63 mm front wall so the glass is 0.5 mm behind the window: the 120 deg view passes the window edges.",
        "Seal 1, window: a 24 x 24 mm piece of clear plastic (cut from the clear lid of the unused 115 x 90 x 55 box), 2 mm thick, in a recess on the OUTSIDE of the front wall, bonded with silicone. Water pressure pushes it onto its seat.",
        "Seal 2, lid: 3 mm silicone foam cord in a groove on the housing rim (33 % squeeze). The lid goes straight on (pegs on the board, lip in the cavity) and is held by two lock bars with no flexing parts: each side of the housing has a solid rail (2.5 mm out, 3 mm thick) and the lid a flange beside it; a rigid C-shaped bar slides down from the top over rail and flange together until its head sits on them. The rail is 0.6 mm thicker at the bottom, so the bar pulls the lid that far onto the cord as it goes home (slope 0.017, far too shallow to back out), and the housing hangs, so gravity keeps the bars down. Press the lid on with a thumb, push the bars down; to open, pull them up by their heads. The bars go in from above, clear of the rack tube.",
        "Seal 3, cable: the board sits ribbon-down (connector at the bottom edge, the usual way up for a Pi camera), so the ribbon leaves the connector straight down and goes through a 20 x 3 mm slot in the floor directly under it, centred on the connector's height behind the PCB: no bend inside the housing. Thread the cable's Pi end through the slot from inside before plugging it into the camera; glue-lined heat-shrink sleeve where it passes the slot; fill the slot with silicone (it faces the ground, so water runs off). Outside, curve it gently forward and zip-tie it along the rack to the box.",
        "Mount: the rack's back tube (wrapped in a strip of inner tube) lies in a 90 deg V along the top of the housing; a cap with a round groove is pulled down by two M3 x 10 screws (heads in counterbores) into blind heat-set inserts, 17 mm apart. Loosen, turn the housing round the tube to aim it level, tighten. The V takes 8-16 mm tubes; the cap groove is cut for the set diameter, so set C_RACK_D to the measured tube and reprint the cap.",
        "Print: housing front face down, lid outer face down, cap top face down, lock bars on their back (open side up); ASA+, 4 walls or more, no supports. Bath test before riding: sealed with a dry tissue inside, 30 min under water.",
        "The ribbon needs a Pi 5 camera cable (22-pin to 15-pin), long enough to run from the back of the rack to the box.",
        "Not included yet: a rain/sun visor (the Wide lens would see one); a ribbon entry into the main box (the flat ribbon does not fit an M16 gland: its own sealed slot in the box)."
      ]
